  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1054 AM CDT Wed Jun 17 2026\n\nAfter the severe threat has passed, Friday morning will remain \nwet until the front passes Friday around noon. The front will cool\nus off a bit and bring us dry conditions for the rest of Friday \nand on Saturday. The previous forecast discussion mentioning the \ntransition into another active pattern faster than expected still \nholds. By Sunday afternoon, increasing rain chances are forecast \nwith additional increases into Monday due to another shortwave \ndisturbance moving into the region. Latest guidance and ensembles \nsuggest heavy rainfall potential. The most recent NBM guidance \ndepicts a 30 to 45 percent chance of two inches or more rainfall \nSunday through Monday, especially across northern portions of \nMiddle Tennessee. It is not a huge concern right now, though it is\nworth mentioning. The rain chances back off on Tuesday and \nWednesday, though the typical summertime afternoon showers and \nstorms will remain.",
